ers feel.&lt;/p&gt;</text><feedback format="html"><text /></feedback></answer><answer fraction="0.0" format="html"><text>&lt;p&gt;Changing narrator access necessarily leaves the voice unchanged.&lt;/p&gt;</text><feedback format="html"><text /></feedback></answer><answer fraction="0.0" format="html"><text>&lt;p&gt;Voice depends on dialogue punctuation rather than narrative perspective.&lt;/p&gt;</text><feedback format="html"><text /></feedback></answer><answer fraction="0.0" format="html"><text>&lt;p&gt;First-person narration requires the same attitude in every story.&lt;/p&gt;</text><feedback format="html"><text /></feedback></answer></question></quiz>